{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 6e1be476: a descriptor read is truthful or unavailable.\n\nConfirmed. Explore gives the runtime's answer or it answers\nunavailable. It never gives an admitted answer from an invented\ndescriptor. The accessor descriptor goes.\n\n1. For represented data, the trap returns the descriptor that the\n   runtime's object has: the same kind, value and three attributes.\n2. A descriptor read of a property with an unrepresented value answers\n   unavailable, with the entry that a direct read of that property\n   gives. It adds no Lack and no result form.\n3. The same rule covers each operation that reads the descriptor\n   through the trap: Object.keys, Object.entries, Object.values,\n   Object.assign, a spread, a for-in loop, JSON.stringify and\n   Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptors. Each is unavailable on an object\n   with such a property, and each is exact on an object with none.\n4. Reflect.ownKeys and the `in` operator stay supported. They give the\n   runtime's answer and expose no value.\n5. The ordinary runtime path and the oracle stay untouched, as you\n   state.\n\nNamed cases, one test each: a descriptor of a represented property\nequals the runtime's in each member. A descriptor read of an\nunrepresented property is unavailable. Object.keys on an object with\nsuch a property is unavailable. Object.keys on an object with none\nequals the runtime's. Reflect.ownKeys equals the runtime's on both.\nOne control: the accessor descriptor makes the first case fail.\n\nNumbers before more source on this slice. By a source read, list each\nsite in the body judgment and in the platform rules that enumerates or\nspreads an object which can hold an unrepresented value. State, for\nGrow, Lending and Counter, which acts on an item with a pending output\nreach one. If a common path reaches one, each dependent exploration\nbecomes unavailable, and the lazy reader then needs another form. Stop\nand report in that case. I add this limit to section 5.4 of the note\nin the amendment after E1.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}